WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.440
Where have you been?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:16.650
For a walk.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:17.610
For a walk?

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.060
Episode 6

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.060
Fierce Battle! School Wars

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.340
Yes, I'll give Chris the message.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.770
Mr. and Mrs. Thorndyke will be coming home this afternoon to see you.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.390
Mom and Dad are coming home?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.360
Isn't that great, Chris?

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.110
I wonder how many months it's been already.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.230
But…

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.780
Is something bothering you?

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.410
No, it's nothing. I'm done.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.950
You haven't finished eating your fruits.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.370
It was delicious, Ella.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.520
If Mom and Dad find out about you, it could be trouble. So…

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.070
We understand. We'll hide.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.860
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.280
Mom and Dad are busy people, so I'm sure they'll leave right away.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.000
Sonic.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.290
Is he angry?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.380
No way.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.010
Never mind that. You better hurry or you'll be late.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.300
Oh no!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.650
Chuck, Chris's dad is your son, right?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.440
Right.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.150
What does he do?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.940
He's the president of an unimaginably large company.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.950
What does Chris's mother do?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.490
She's a movie star.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.840
His mom and dad are so busy that they rarely get to see Chris.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:40.800
Yeah.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.090
Poor thing.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.370
Splash! Rustle rustle...

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.040
This is no time to be relaxing to the sound of the waves.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.460
If I'm admired, I'll be able to conquer the world. That means I need to gain admiration.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:24.380
So in order to gain admiration, I'll teach the children to admire me.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:25.380
Hey!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.050
Here you go.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.060
Which one would be best... This one!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.730
Here we go.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.530
This is it!

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.400
What the heck?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:26.400
How are we supposed to solve these? I don't understand them at all.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:33.200
Multiply and... I don't know what to do. Sheesh!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.080
Ta-daa! Good morning!

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.050
You're also supposed to say “Good morning!”

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.130
Who are you?

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.010
Teacher robot E-51.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.100
Teacher robot?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.720
I will be the teacher starting today.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.230
What about me?

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.270
Out.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:03.230
Out?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:04.940
Out!

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.200
What a rude robot!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.030
I'm going to tell the principal on him.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.580
Delicious.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.500
Principal!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:36.010
He had the nerve to tell me, the homeroom teacher, to get out and threw me out of the classroom.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.560
You must warn him strictly.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:50.780
Even difficult math can be easy if you solve it with a smile!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.950
I'm starting to feel the same way.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:54.490
Me too.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.490
Same here.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.620
Me too!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.290
What a wonderful lesson.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.880
You should learn from him too, Mr. Stewart.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.550
Aww man...

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.220
Education is love.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:24.440
That robot is suspicious. I'm contacting the intelligence agency.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.710
This is code name Teacher.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.920
This is code name Teacher. Do you read me?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.840
A robot has taken over a classroom?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.550
And you want us to send the land, sea and air troops to destroy it?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.090
Yes, on the double.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.400
Stop messing around, you punk!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:18.320
You don't have to get mad like that. I guess I'll just have to tell the police.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.460
Hello?

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:29.170
What? A robot is holding students hostage?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.800
I'll be right there so wait for me in front of the school gate.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.050
What's taking him so long? He's late... There he is!

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.060
Hurry hurry hurry!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.440
This way!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.610
The students are in big trouble!

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.150
Over here! Please hurry up!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:58.660
Huh?

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.700
Oh yeah. It's time for P.E, so they‘re out on the field.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.790
For P.E. today, we're going to play baseball.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:18.130
The basics of baseball is playing catch. Okay, let's start!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.220
There he is.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.310
That's the robot that's holding the students hostage. Hurry up and arrest him.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:34.070
Relax your wrists and elbows. Relax.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.320
From the looks of it, he's getting along with the students. There's no trouble.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.530
I see no reason to arrest him.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.830
This is not the time to be eating!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.290
How dare you steal from the police!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.000
You're under arrest!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.210
Give me back my hamburger!

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.040
Wait! Give me back my hamburger!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:07.600
I'll use satellite communication to check how E-51 is teaching the children to admire me.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.690
Let's see.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.400
You can do it, Teacher!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:14.480
Come on! You can do it, Teacher!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.480
Come on!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.650
Chris, right here.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.580
Perfect pitch for me!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.500
Wow!

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.010
Mr. E-51 is the best! I admire you!

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:45.010
I did it! A homerun! I did it! Hooray!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.740
Oh my, he's really friendly with the students!

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.280
That's good.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.500
There's no point if E-51 is the one who's being admired instead of me!

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.910
Welcome home.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:48.990
We're home.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.790
Nelson, Lindsey.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.210
Dad.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.090
Father. I'm glad that you look well.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.300
It's a miracle that you're both home together.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.050
Stop exaggerating.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.390
That's Chris' mom and dad?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.690
They're both cool-looking. Did you see them, Sonic?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:21.820
Sheesh.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.030
Good job, Danny!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:29.990
Is it a home run?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.670
Diving catch.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.630
Mr. E-51?!

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.550
Wow, cool.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.180
I did it! I must be awesome!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.890
Woohoo!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.440
E-51.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.230
Messenger Robo.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.480
There's a message for you from Dr. Eggman.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:06.700
What is it?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.160
Don't get carried away, you bastard!

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.280
Was Dr. Eggman angry?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:16.790
He was. He said that you forgot your important job of getting the students to admire him!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.540
Oh, I completely forgot about it.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:22.920
What's wrong with you!

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.210
I learned something.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:26.970
Learned what?

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:34.310
Instead of getting the students to admire Dr. Eggman, it feels a lot better to be admired myself.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.770
Are you sure you want to say that?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:41.060
I'm going to tell Dr. Eggman on you and you're going to have to bear the consequences!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.150
What's the matter, Mr. E-51?

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:51.450
No matter what Dr. Eggman does, I will protect my students since that's my duty as a teacher.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:57.160
I don't know what's going on, but I'm starting to admire you more and more, Mr. E-51.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:58.710
Me too.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:14:59.920
Same here.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.590
It feels so good.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:12.050
You're being respected? If you're going to act like that, then I'm going to get sulky.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.970
Sulk, sulk...

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:15.810
Oh my.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.310
He's sulking.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.520
I'm really angry now!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.700
That's all for today.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.080
I have to rush home.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.040
What's up?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.250
Mom and Dad are coming home after a long absence.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.640
E-51!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.640
Dr. Eggman?

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.060
How dare you ignore my important orders and get yourself admired instead.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:02.690
I'm going to scrap you!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:07.020
Sssssssscrap. You can't!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.150
Chris, help me.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:17.370
But teacher, you said that no matter what Dr. Eggman does, it's your duty as a teacher to protect your students!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.740
Did I say that?

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.910
You did!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.660
Yeah, you said so!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:28.210
So I did say that? Then I guess it can't be helped.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.260
What's so funny, Eggman?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:37.050
You guys are fools for easily believing what a teacher says.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:41.640
You're all staying after school to study and can't go home until you respect me!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:43.350
No way...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.640
What?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:49.690
E-51! Begin the after-school class if you don't want to be scrapped!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.360
Yes, sir!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.570
You've gotta be kidding. I'm going home!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:03.580
Wait. Chris, I will not permit you to be the only one allowed to go home.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.760
He should be home by now.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.600
I wonder if he's gotten into an accident.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.270
If so, my guard service would contact me.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:28.440
You're right. It's only natural for parents to worry about their child when waiting for him to come home.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.780
School just ended.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.610
Maybe it's better if I go pick him up.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:42.790
It's Mr. and Mrs. Thorndyke's rule that Chris get to and from school just like other normal children.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.460
I really should go pick him up.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.420
Dear, let's trust Chris.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:56.970
Oh sorry. I have to control myself, or else, I'll be called an overbearing parent.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.590
That won't do Chris any good.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.930
He loves his child too much.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.270
They seem very worried.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:06.600
Sonic.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.270
Isn't there anything you can do?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:29.250
Students, draw a beautiful sketch of Dr. Eggman.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:36.010
By drawing a beautiful sketch of Dr. Eggman, feelings of admiration will grow within you.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:41.220
How's this pose? Or is this better?

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.100
It's impossible to draw a beautiful picture of Eggman.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:54.190
What? What?

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.900
What is going on?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.240
I think this pose is better after all.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:05.990
Dr. Eggman, this is no time to be posing.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.750
Eggman, enough with the games.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:15.590
E-51?

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:16.170
Yes.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:17.880
Get rid of Sonic!

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.510
Sonic?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.470
Yes, sir! Study attack!

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:33.610
C'mon!

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.260
He's strong!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.220
Yeah.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.970
How dare you! Hey, Sonic.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.680
What?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:14.190
I'll give you an Eggman super sticker in commemoration of today's battle.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.150
I don't want that. No, thank you.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.490
Then I'll give it to the kids.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.030
We don't want it either.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.160
Me neither.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:28.540
Same here.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:35.330
Fine. Then I'll put it on myself and leave. Bye!

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.170
What was that about?

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.130
Beats me.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.760
We'll never figure out what Eggman is thinking.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.970
Chris, you better hurry home.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.720
Oh, that's right!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.650
He's really cool.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:56.980
He's wonderful.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:10.330
This day made me think what it truly means to be a teacher.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.160
Don't eat my hamburger!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.550
Wait, you punk!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.840
Give it back to me! Give it back!

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.220
C'mon, aren't you over this by now? Give it back to me! Give it back!

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.300
Give it back to me! Give it back!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.100
Mom, Dad - I'm home!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.440
Chris!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.940
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.610
You're late. Did you go somewhere after school with your friends?

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.530
Uh, just for a bit with Danny and some others...

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.700
No, I wasn't the least bit worried.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:58.710
I also used to wander around when I was your age.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.380
Right. That's natural for kids to do.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:07.180
Whatever.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:11.760
They were so worried that they were one step away from sending the army!

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:13.390
Right, Tanaka?

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:16.600
Yes, I already informed the President about it.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:17.730
What?

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:22.270
It's true. Mrs. Thorndyke contacted all the TV stations for a special news report.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.900
